Verification: a real format-1 RocksDB checkpoint image is opened through `RocksDB.openReadOnly`. The physical inspector enforces finite file/byte bounds, exact column-family inventory, empty default column family with checked iterator status, manifest file length/checksum equality, and exact Store format/Shard/db identity/incarnation, checkpoint ID, applied source position, and mutation sequence. The state inventory scans every registered Column Family under finite record/byte/time bounds; it counts key-kind prefixes, decodes old Message status, terminal generation summaries, and retired identity records, and checks each Message key/source route belongs to the checkpoint Shard. For typed SCHEDULED records it rebuilds and verifies the due/ordered key from Message and source fields, then checks the persisted DUE/ORDERED and EXPIRY values. Each Message and terminal-summary `AttemptObligationRef` uses the bounded point-read budget to fetch and verify its `PublishAttemptLedger` Message ID, generation and canonical obligation ref; missing or mismatched ledgers return stable owner-bound conflicts. It scans recognized INFLIGHT Attempt ledger keys, checks key/value identity and Shard/source identity, and reports unreferenced ledgers as stable ATTEMPT conflicts. It scans INFLIGHT Claim records, validates Claim encoding/key identity, Shard and source Store incarnation, and matches them to the current Message status/generation/current work kind/claim ID; missing, orphan, duplicate and mis-key Claims produce stable conflicts. For same-generation terminal rows, it compares summary status, complete open-obligation list and possible-duplicate flag with the current Message, and reports a terminal Message without a summary; retained summaries for earlier generations are not treated as conflicts. It reports conservative per-Message disposition counts and stable blockers for claimed, SCHEDULED messages with open Attempt obligations, unresolved send, handoff and terminal states. Missing timeline indexes return a stable conflict bound to the old Message key digest and canonical source position. The manifest-bound physical inventory is checked before and after the logical scan. Tests cover valid timeline indexes, a missing expiry-index conflict, malformed Message rejection without file changes, read-budget exhaustion, matching and missing Message Attempt ledgers, matching/missing/mismatched terminal summaries, terminal-summary Attempt ownership, an unreferenced Attempt ledger, conservative disposition mapping, a manifest/image mismatch, and valid/missing/orphan/mis-key Claim records.

Commands:
`./gradlew test --tests 'com.nereusstream.delay.store.LegacyCheckpointImageInspectorTest' checkstyleTest`

`./gradlew test --tests 'com.nereusstream.delay.store.LegacyCheckpointImageInspectorTest' --tests 'com.nereusstream.delay.store.LegacyCheckpointClaimInventoryTest' checkstyleTest`

`./gradlew checkDocumentation`

`./gradlew checkstyleMain`

Result: `LegacyCheckpointImageInspectorTest` 6/6 and `LegacyCheckpointClaimInventoryTest` 1/1 with 0 failures/errors/skips; terminal tests cover matching, missing and mismatched same-generation summaries. `checkstyleTest`, `checkDocumentation`, `git diff --check`, and `jq empty docs/ndip/NDIP-3/progress.json` passed on this revision. `./gradlew checkstyleMain` reports only pre-existing 123-character lines in untouched `PersistentLaneScheduler.java:1327` and `TargetWorkerHostRuntime.java:347`.

Scope: this proves physical identity and a partial bounded Message/inventory audit. It checks typed SCHEDULED timeline/expiry indexes, reports conservative status dispositions, verifies Message and terminal-summary Attempt forward references, detects unreferenced recognized INFLIGHT Attempt ledgers, checks Claim identity against current Message and Store incarnation, and compares same-generation terminal Message/summary status, obligations and duplicate marker. Historical terminal/Floor/retention relationships, live Owner lease/policy/Claim precondition authority, Admission/Journal or other owner/proof relationships, old TimelineEntry/Profile semantics, Lane control, source replay, the full per-Shard dry-run report, durable activation, conversion, rollback and reader retirement remain outside this slice. B6 remains `IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION`.

